## JSON-LD Interop Phase 1 (OWL export/import, SPARQL CONSTRUCT, MCP)

Context:
OntoBricks already spoke RDF via Turtle/RDF-XML, but external systems and LLM
agents prefer JSON-LD. Phase 1 adds JSON-LD as an opt-in serialization for OWL
export/import, SPARQL CONSTRUCT/DESCRIBE results, and the MCP describe_ontology
tool, without changing default Turtle / tabular-row behaviour.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/w3c/owl/iri.py
   Added serialize_graph(turtle|json-ld) with shared IRI-safe escaping; serialize_turtle delegates to it.
2. src/back/core/w3c/owl/OntologyGenerator.py
   generate(output_format=...) serializes via serialize_graph.
3. src/back/objects/ontology/Owl.py, Ontology.py
   generate_owl accepts output_format (turtle default, json-ld).
4. src/api/routers/internal/ontology.py
   GET /export-owl?format=turtle|json-ld.
5. src/back/core/w3c/owl/OntologyParser.py
   Accepts json-ld; extracted _salvage_truncated_owl so JSON documents are not mangled.
6. src/back/core/w3c/sparql/SparqlQueryRunner.py, DomainQueryService.py
   output_format=json-ld for CONSTRUCT/DESCRIBE; ValidationError on SELECT/ASK.
7. src/api/routers/v1.py
   QueryModel.output_format; response may include jsonld.
8. src/api/routers/domains.py
   GET /domain/ontology?format=json-ld; helper _owl_document_for_domain.
9. src/mcp-server/server/tools.py
   describe_ontology requests and displays OWL (JSON-LD).
10. tests/units/ontology/test_owl_jsonld.py, test_rdf_utils.py
    Export/import isomorphic round-trip and parse_rdf_flexible json-ld case.
11. tests/units/core/test_sparql_jsonld.py
    CONSTRUCT json-ld, limit, SELECT rejection, rows default.
12. tests/units/mcp/test_domain_policy_gating.py
    Mock ontology payload and assertions updated for JSON-LD.
13. docs/api.md, docs/mcp.md, docs/architecture.md, docs/user-guide.md, README.md
    Document format=json-ld / output_format and MCP JSON-LD behaviour.

