## Stop ghost Not Mapped relationship paths on Mapping Visual

Context:
Opening Mapping Studio → Visual could render a duplicate canvas for a few
seconds. `MappingStudioTabs.show()` called `_onShown` both directly and via
Bootstrap `shown.bs.tab`, scheduling two concurrent `initMappingDesigner` runs.
Each appended an SVG, but cleanup only removed the first `:scope > svg`,
leaving a ghost layer until a later re-init cleared one of them.
Note: this was first suspected to explain the red "not mapped" relationships,
but it did not; the real cause is fixed in the "Keep hidden entities and
relationships when unmapping" section below.

Changes:

1. src/front/static/mapping/js/mapping-design.js
   - `show()` only calls `_onShown` when the tab is already active (otherwise
     Bootstrap's `shown.bs.tab` owns the call).
   - `initMappingDesigner` uses a sequence token so superseded concurrent runs
     abort after awaits.
   - Clears all canvas SVGs/legends/empty messages, not just the first SVG.
2. tests/units/front/test_mapping_visual_ghost_links.py (new)
   Contract tests for the double-`_onShown` guard, multi-SVG cleanup, and
   init sequence token.

