## Fix numeric set-attribute literals for Postgres Lakebase

Context:
Applying business rule ActiveContract100Points on Jacob Martin (CUST0000037)
failed with "Business rule 'ActiveContract100Points' failed to run". Postgres
rejected `object = 100` with `operator does not exist: text = integer`, because
set-attribute consequents such as `loyaltypoints(?x, 100)` emitted a bare integer
into the flat triple `object` column (text), both in the SELECT and in the
exact-dedup NOT EXISTS.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/reasoning/shacl_rules/ShaclFlatSqlBackend.py
   `_literal_object_sql` quotes bare numeric tokens as string literals (`'100'`)
   for the text object column; built-in comparisons stay unquoted via
   `literal_sql` / `_resolve_arg`.
2. tests/units/reasoning/test_if_then_to_shacl_regression.py
   Contract flipped: numeric set-attribute objects must be quoted; asserts no bare
   integer in the SELECT or NOT EXISTS.

