## Materialise set-attribute literals from entity business rules

Context:
Entity business-rule runs (ActiveContract100Points / PendingContract10KPoints on
Jacob Martin) inferred loyaltypoints triples but wrote nothing: the write path
filtered through `uri_triples`, which drops literal objects, so set-attribute
consequents never reached the graph. Replace semantics are applied so a new
literal value supersedes the previous one.

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinInferredMaterialize.py
   Added `writable_triples` (URI subject/predicate, non-empty object: literal or URI).
   `uri_triples` is unchanged and still feeds the batch Delta/graph path.
2. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/node/NodeBusinessRuleService.py
   Materialises through `writable_triples`; before insert, clears prior `(s, p, *)`
   for literal attributes via `delete_subject_predicate` when the store exposes it,
   otherwise selects the current objects and deletes them exactly via `delete_triples`.
3. tests/units/dtwin/test_entity_business_rules.py
   Covers literal set-attribute materialisation and the replace pairs.
4. tests/units/dtwin/test_v090_twin_build_prepare.py
   `writable_triples` keeps literal objects; `uri_triples` remains URI-only.

