## Patterns: persist the entity universe so Coverage works on saved runs

Context:
Coverage was still empty because the detail view is a saved run, and the saved
catalog did not store the entity universe (anchor_count) — so the percentage
could not be computed. The universe is now persisted into the saved snapshot
and exposed as run-level stats, so Coverage renders on saved runs too.

Changes:
1. src/back/core/graph_analysis/pattern/saved_pattern_sql.py
   Added anchor_count to _SAVED_COLUMNS and to both INSERTs (catalog SELECT and
   the bulk rest INSERT, via a new anchor_count parameter).
2. src/back/core/graph_analysis/pattern/SavedPatternStore.py
   Added anchor_count to _KPI_COLUMNS (auto-migrates existing saved tables) and
   the CREATE TABLE DDL. save() reads anchor_count from the run summary (via a
   separate, column-tolerant query) and threads it into the per-pattern metrics
   and insert_rest_sql. patterns() now selects max(anchor_count), sums support
   for covered, and returns a run-level stats block
   {anchor_count, covered_count, pattern_count}.
3. src/front/static/intelligence/js/intelligence-patterns.js
   _showPendingSaved prefers the snapshot's own stats (when anchor_count is
   present) and otherwise falls back to the freshly-computed run stats.
4. tests/units/core/test_saved_pattern_store.py
   Fixture summary gained anchor_count; asserts patterns().stats carries
   anchor_count / covered_count / pattern_count.

Note:
Runs saved before this change have no stored anchor_count → Coverage stays "—"
for them; re-running Detect produces a snapshot with the universe. A browser
hard refresh is needed to pick up the new static assets.

